  "findings": [
    "The only two test-body changes patch the existing subprocess.Popen.__init__ method instead of replacing the Popen class. The identical forbidden callable still raises pytest.fail for any attempted process construction.",
    "The actual class remains available for asyncio.windows_utils.Popen inheritance. Its super().__init__ lookup reaches the patched method while the sentinel is active and the original method after monkeypatch restores it; no temporary substitute base class is cached.",
    "CPython 3.11.9 defines Popen._child_created=False on the class and __del__ returns before other fields when no child was created, so a forbidden initializer cannot cause partially initialized destructor work.",
    "The same tests still perform actual EvidenceStore load/add and actual controller/store I/O while both execution and runtime discovery sentinels remain active. All existing assertions, decorator values, function names and other file bytes remain exact.",
    "Focused helper changes only the two accepted test hashes; workflow changes only one helper hash. Data6797, native1a035, fixture729, source/installed147, native75/14, all48pins/36origins and original deadlines are unchanged."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Static source/API review only; no pytest, parser, native or same-head PASS claim.",
    "Actual E failures remain failures. Corrected execution is still required."
  ]
